// After a split the upper packet is completed first. Pending lower pieces are
// ancestors of that packet, so crossing them cannot violate tower capacity.

// A split DP treats resident towers as background. Do not permanently
// absorb those residents at an event when that would destroy the gain.
// Complete the original packet instead; background towers stay intact.

// Between two cells without home returns, concatenating one tower bottom-up
// and the other top-down preserves the word. Only their height boundary moves.
// Keep the net transfer at its first position; intervening operations commute
// exactly when neither endpoint has been touched. Passing over a cell is safe.

// The last original departure from the net donor left at least
